    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Algerian resistance, led primarily by the FLN, began its armed struggle in 1954 with the launch of \"Alger Open,\" marking the official start of the war against French colonial forces. Key flashpoints often highlighted from the Algerian perspective include the brutal racial laws enforced by France, which denied rights and fueled deep-seated resentment among the local population. The group's eventual victory in December 1962 was celebrated not just as a political liberation, but as a fundamental humanization of the populace previously oppressed by the colonial system. Although international recognition for independence took some years later, this timeline emphasizes the relentless 12-year effort to reclaim sovereignty and dignity.",
      "source": "target",
