      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that. so if we're looking at it from a historical lens, was there actually any nuance in the French position, or was the \"stability and development\" argument just a pretext for maintaining the power structure? i'm trying to figure out if historians generally see their justifications as legitimate arguments for the time or if they're viewed as inherently dishonest.",
